I recently got my hands on the upcoming  third installment of The Witcher series  The Wild Hunt and I can safely say that  if like me you enjoyed its predecessor  assassins of Kings this latest offering  plays vastly the same only set free in a  massive and detailed open-world which is  good news for more detailed look and  chat about what we actually played want  to go check out this other video I made  with mark but what if you've never  played a Witcher game before how'd you  know if CD Projekt Reds latest offering  is your cup of need well I have one  question for you do you like Game of  Thrones now stay with me you see it  dawned on me while playing that these  two fantasy worlds are extremely similar  in many important ways and I'm talking  way beyond superficial things like  swords British accents and beards what's  wrong with my beard nothing girl your  beard is lovely now ish I listen to my  eleven reasons why The Witcher 3 might  be the closest thing we're ever going to  get to a truly great Game of Thrones  RPG  don't be fooled by the beautiful and  varied environments that greet you in  The Witcher 3 this world is ugly brutal  and dangerous death prejudice and  betrayal are every bit as common as the  peasant soldiers and monsters they call  at home it is such a savage place in  fact that it can be hard to imagine how  anyone beyond the rich and fortunate can  eke out a living here remind you of  anywhere  this gritty flavor is echoed in the  tales told in The Witcher Universe now  this point we know very little about the  story of three but based on its heritage  it's clear that storytelling is valued  as highly as gameplay by the folks CD  Projekt RED this manifests in the game  with complex narratives and detailed  characterization at its core whether  this is executed as well as in George RR  Martin's offering is up for debate but  if you like experiences which are as  much about story as they are about  actual fighting then my guess is The  Witcher 3 will likely not disappoint  as with Game of Thrones a shrewd  politician in the world of The Witcher  can be as deadly as the most heavily  armored foe though you play mostly as  Geralt the infamous silver-haired  Witcher who doesn't engage directly in  politics through him your actions do  make an impact on the political  landscape this was certainly the case in  The Witcher 2 anyway and based on the  initial sequence I got my hands on we  can expect much more of this to come in  the Wild Hunt  morale matters are rarely black and  white in both Game of Thrones and The  Witcher as the witcher geralt you are  frequently given decisions with a moral  component these are not labored or even  labelled as in some RPGs they're more  subtle do you reject payment for helping  someone who you now suspect to be a liar  and possibly a murderer or do you take  that coin and upgrade your weapons to  aid in the killing of a menacing Griffon  for the greater good of the town  morality in this game you see is all  shades of gray and speaking of shades of  gray like George RR Martin's epic tale  there are as many as sexy encounter to  be had in The Witcher 3 if the first  hours are anything to go by literally  the opening cutscene is both abstract  and but tacular this is not mere sex  position however according to the  developers more of a storytelling device  to reveal the complex relationships  between the key characters and their  butts if you enjoy all the gore in Game  of Thrones then The Witcher 3 should  certainly satisfy your bloodlust the  trailers have hinted at this mature  total ready  and by hinted I mean this crow exploring  at the back of a man's head  Wow this Gore factor is present in game  too frequently Garrett's killing slice  will lop off an arm a head or even a  wing the client of Steel on steel is a  familiar sound in The Witcher 3 and like  Game of Thrones  the fighting doesn't stand on pomp and  ceremony it's brutal fast and deadly  less fancy swashbuckling are more nasty  squash buckling your limbs did that work  close enough onwards combat isn't only  about weapons magic too exists in the  world of The Witcher as Geralt you can  cast signs to aid you in battle  these range from great balls of fire to  protective shields however if you're  drawn to the world of Westeros because  of its subtle inclusion of magic then  don't let this put you off The Witcher  magic is woven into the game setting  more of a strange strand of the fabric  of life than an OTT power that everyone  wields giants dragons and White Walkers  it's fair to say the game of Thrones is  fond of monsters and if deadly mythical  creatures is your bag then once again  The Witcher will deliver as a Witcher  it's Geralt job to have these jerks good  thing too as the world is crawling with  them granted it's not quite a dragon but  hey this Gryphon is still pretty  impressive  ah  Daenerys she used to be my favorite you  know at the beginning and then her story  just went a bit mad this is just me  anyway she's a big deal in Game of  Thrones arguably the main character a  Targaryen princess with white blond hair  some call her mother of dragons the  chosen one way way way way  that's not Danny that's ciri she is both  Geralt sward and a Witcher in training  she was also a second playable character  in The Witcher 3 set to be a crucial  piece in the game's main storyline oh  yeah Charles dance is actually in them  both and his voice is just the best have  a listen I shall give her what she  deserves  oh and one more special bonus for you  guys it appears I'm not the first person  to notice this similarity when playing  the game traveling the wilds I overheard  two peasants discussing a horrific event  that happened recently something they  called the red funeral the less said  about that the better  anyway let me know if you're excited for  The Witcher 3 and if you can spot any  other similarities between these two  fantasy realms leave me a comment or hit  me up on Twitter and come back to  Gainesville comm for more on the Witcher  3  you
 

